 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Proportional to the number of intersected octants. The algorithm has moderate initial cost for computing and sorting mid-plane intersections, but subsequent traversal is trivial [S3, S5]. In the worst case (ray passing through all occupied nodes), it is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of nodes [G].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Proportional to the number of intersected octants [S3]. The algorithm has moderate initial cost for computing and sorting mid-plane intersections, but subsequent traversal is trivial [S3]. In the worst case (ray passing through all occupied nodes), it is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of nodes [G].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** $O(D)$ where $D$ is the depth of the octree, due to recursion stack [G].
 *   **Strengths:** Efficient for sparse data; avoids sampling empty space; returns intersected octants in sorted order (closest first) [S4, unofficial]. It is faster on average than sphere marching because it utilizes empty octree nodes with smaller average depth, despite requiring more iterations [S2].
